WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.001 --> 00:00:05.035
Attorney dashboard overview: a guided tour in eight chapters.

2
00:00:05.035 --> 00:00:07.972
Chapter 1: Getting started. Your dashboard, profile and firm in one place.

3
00:00:07.972 --> 00:00:15.296
Sign in and the sidebar splits Lead Generation from Case Management.

4
00:00:15.297 --> 00:00:22.646
Keep your profile, practice areas and service area current: they drive routing.

5
00:00:22.646 --> 00:00:29.473
Firm admins manage attorneys, staff and roles from the firm dashboard.

6
00:00:29.474 --> 00:00:32.407
Chapter 2: Receiving and accepting cases. Review routed matches before you decide.

7
00:00:32.407 --> 00:00:40.680
New matches arrive here with value, strength and a countdown to respond.

8
00:00:40.680 --> 00:00:50.638
Open a match for a read-only review: incident, treatment, insurance and evidence.

9
00:00:50.639 --> 00:00:57.187
Accept or decline when you are ready. Accepting charges the routing fee.

10
00:00:57.187 --> 00:01:04.923
Accepted matches move to Active Cases with a next action for each.

11
00:01:04.923 --> 00:01:07.923
Chapter 3: The case workspace. Everything about a matter, grouped into tabs.

12
00:01:07.923 --> 00:01:17.238
Each case opens on a summary: value, policy limits, demand and days open.

13
00:01:17.238 --> 00:01:23.747
Client info keeps contact details and parties in one place.

14
00:01:23.747 --> 00:01:30.175
Activity is a running timeline of everything that happened on the case.

15
00:01:30.175 --> 00:01:36.174
Medical, Claim and Documents tabs hold the evidence behind the case.

16
00:01:36.174 --> 00:01:39.098
Chapter 4: Tasks and workflows. Know what is next on every matter.

17
00:01:39.098 --> 00:01:47.521
The case Tasks queue lists recommended next steps and open items.

18
00:01:47.521 --> 00:01:54.923
Workflow shows the case moving through phases and stages.

19
00:01:54.923 --> 00:02:02.414
The Tasks hub rolls up every case so nothing slips.

20
00:02:02.414 --> 00:02:09.270
Firm admins define the standard workflow new matters follow.

21
00:02:09.270 --> 00:02:12.196
Chapter 5: Client communication. Messages, mentions and contact details.

22
00:02:12.196 --> 00:02:19.539
Messages collects client and adjuster threads across every case.

23
00:02:19.539 --> 00:02:25.964
Team and Mentions tabs keep internal conversation separate.

24
00:02:25.964 --> 00:02:31.974
From any case, Message client opens the conversation for that matter.

25
00:02:31.974 --> 00:02:34.899
Chapter 6: E-signatures and firm templates. Retainers and authorizations, signed electronically.

26
00:02:34.899 --> 00:02:43.139
Signatures tracks the retainer and HIPAA authorization for each case.

27
00:02:43.139 --> 00:02:50.470
Documents & E-sign shows outstanding requests and signatures firm-wide.

28
00:02:50.470 --> 00:02:57.303
Firm templates store reusable retainers, HIPAA forms and intake packages.

29
00:02:57.303 --> 00:03:00.217
Chapter 7: Demand, negotiation and settlement. The Resolution tab carries the case to close.

30
00:03:00.217 --> 00:03:09.353
Demand checks readiness and assembles specials, liability and damages.

31
00:03:09.353 --> 00:03:16.726
Negotiation logs offers and counteroffers against your demand.

32
00:03:16.726 --> 00:03:23.568
Settlement records the outcome, disbursement and closing steps.

33
00:03:23.568 --> 00:03:26.493
Chapter 8: Billing, time and invoices. Track time, invoices and your platform billing.

34
00:03:26.493 --> 00:03:33.827
Log team hours on each case for profitability and fee petitions.

35
00:03:33.827 --> 00:03:41.159
Invoices tracks client invoices and payments for the case.

36
00:03:41.159 --> 00:03:48.518
The Billing hub rolls up fees collected across every case.

37
00:03:48.518 --> 00:03:54.944
Firm Time & Billing sets billing rates and reviews time entries.

38
00:03:54.944 --> 00:04:00.896
Attorney billing covers your plan, payment method and routing fees.

39
00:04:00.896 --> 00:04:05.407
That is the tour. Each chapter has a written guide with steps and tips under Help > Guides.
